The address-bar verification badge.

The badge shows the **weakest link**. The bytes of a page may hash correctly
and the badge may still say `claim only`: if the name resolution carried no
proof, the page on screen may not belong to the name that was asked for. Byte
verification does not answer that question, and the badge must not hide the
difference.

No lock icon is used. A lock means "the transport is protected", which is not
what this browser is saying; reusing the same icon for a different meaning
would corrupt a meaning users spent years learning.

